@startuml wt_setup_changes
title Setup with a fixed WT roster
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 75
actor "Users" as U
participant "STs" as ST
participant "Boomlets" as B
participant "Nisos" as N
participant "Initial WT" as W
participant "Bound SARs" as S
participant "Iso and inactive backups" as Backup

legend left
Grouped lifelines represent five independent peers.
Green notes identify setup additions for WT failover.
endlegend

group Roster and parameter agreement
  N -> B: Ordered signed peer records, WT identities,\nmilestone blocks and descriptor parameters
  B -> B: Verify five peer identities and matching parameters
  B -> ST: Authenticated, nonce-bound setup review
  ST -> U: Display ordered WT identities and setup parameters
  U -> ST: Approve
  ST -> B: Signed setup review
  B -> B: Verify review and derive setup_instance_id
  B -> N: Signed parameter fingerprint
  N -> B: Five matching parameter signatures
  B -> B: Complete PARAMETERS_AGREED
  note over ST,B #E8F5E9
    One to five distinct WT keys and identities.
    Preserve the reviewed order and full addresses.
    The setup ID commits the roster.
  end note
end

group Initial WT authority
  B -> B: Store active_wt_index = 0
  B -> B: Store genesis head derived from version and setup ID
  N -> W: Signed setup records and parameter agreement
  W -> N: Registration invoices when payment is due
  U -> N: Payment evidence
  N -> W: Payment evidence
  W -> B: Setup registration receipt through Niso
  B -> B: Verify local receipt
  B -> N: Signed WT-ready checkpoint
  N -> B: Five matching checkpoint signatures
  B -> B: Complete WT_READY
  note over B,W #E8F5E9
    Enroll the first roster WT for setup.
    Dormant registration is optional.
    State-advancing WT traffic authenticates the active head.
  end note
end

group SAR finalization and backup
  B -> W: Signed bound SAR identity and encrypted SAR setup request
  W -> S: Forward to each exact bound SAR
  S -> W: Signed finalization evidence encrypted to each Boomlet
  W -> B: Authenticated local finalization evidence
  B -> B: Verify own SAR and WT evidence
  B -> N: Signed SAR-ready checkpoint
  N -> B: Five matching checkpoint signatures
  B -> B: Complete SAR_READY
  B -> Backup: Authenticated, target-bound backup state
  Backup -> B: Signed backup receipt
  B -> N: Signed backup-ready checkpoint after local receipt checks
  N -> B: Five matching checkpoint signatures
  B -> B: Complete BACKUP_READY
  note over B,Backup #E8F5E9
    Backup replay state includes the active head, index,
    and authoritative switch journal.
    Source revocation and journal recovery gate backup activation.
  end note
end
@enduml
